          "en": "could be their own component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 118.89,
          "en": "Could be, you don't have to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.89,
          "end": 120.19,
          "en": "You will learn throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.19,
          "end": 122.85,
          "en": "how I approach the splitting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.85,
          "end": 125.94800000000001,
          "en": "up of an application into separate components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.94800000000001,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "We also have, of course our main area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.34,
          "en": "and the sidebar here as components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.34,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "And that is the core idea behind Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "Build components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139,
          "en": "Each component has its own template, its own HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "maybe its own styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "and more importantly also its own business logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "And this is the great benefit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "It allows you to split up your complex application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 154.07999999999998,
          "en": "your complex webpage into reusable parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.07999999999998,
          "end": 156.135,
          "en": "You may use a component more than once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.135,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "and that allows you to easily replicate that business logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 162.72,
          "en": "replicate that styling, or in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.72,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "make a finally controlled piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "in your your application without having to crunch everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 173.31,
          "en": "into one single script file one single HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.31,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "Instead, it's very easy to update.",
